  <section>
    <h2>Method overview</h2>
    <p>BM25-V bridges text retrieval and visual search through three ideas:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Sparse visual words.</strong> A frozen SigLIP2 ViT extracts 729 patch-level
        features (1152-dim each). A Sparse Autoencoder projects each patch into 18,432
        dims and applies ReLU + top-<em>k</em> sparsification, keeping only
        <em>k</em>=16 active visual words per patch.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Term frequency via sum-pooling.</strong> Sparse patch vectors are
        sum-pooled across all patches into one image-level vector; activation magnitude
        serves as TF — visual words that fire across many patches get higher TF.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>BM25 scoring with IDF.</strong> IDF is computed from the gallery,
        down-weighting pervasive background features and amplifying rare discriminative
        ones. Scoring follows the standard Okapi BM25 formula via sparse matrix
        multiplication on inverted posting lists.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      The <strong>two-stage pipeline</strong> combines BM25-V (fast sparse first stage,
      top-200 candidates) with dense cosine reranking, recovering near-exact dense
      accuracy while providing interpretable attribution.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
